---
import RichText from '../RichText.astro';
import { business, brands, whatsappSend } from '../../data/business.js';
import { brandList } from '../../lib/format.js';
---
<details class="opt-notes">
  <summary>Placement, brands and how the quote works</summary>
  <div class="opt-notes-body">
    <p>The indoor unit can sit high on a wall, or on the floor if a wall is taken up by windows. The outdoor unit needs a sensible spot: somewhere it can be fixed securely, where the pipes can run neatly, and where the noise will not sit under a neighbour’s bedroom window.</p>
    <p>If you want more than one room, a multi-room system connects two, three or four indoor units to a single outdoor unit. You can set each room on its own. It avoids a row of outdoor units along the wall.</p>
    <p>We install {brandList(brands)}. You can see and hear them at the showroom on {business.street}, {business.town}, before you decide. Mitsubishi Electric publish a low noise figure from 19dB for some of their indoor units. That is their figure for those models, not a promise that every room will measure 19dB once the unit is fitted.</p>
    <p><RichText text={`Send photos, measurements and a floor plan of the rooms and the outside wall. ${whatsappSend}. We quote remotely from those. A survey is only if it is needed.`} /></p>
  </div>
</details>

<style>
  .opt-notes {
    margin-top: 28px;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }
  .opt-notes summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .opt-notes summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .opt-notes summary::after {
    content: '+';
    float: right;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  .opt-notes[open] summary::after { content: '–'; }
  .opt-notes-body { padding: 0 20px 18px; }
  .opt-notes-body p { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 12px; }
</style>
